<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volsella</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vuls-</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volsilla</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a kind of pincers</i> for pulling out
			hairs, <i>tweezers.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Curc. 4, 4, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 28, 5</span></i>.—As a
			surgical instrument, <i>forceps</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 7,
				12, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 18,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pugnare volsellis, non gladio,</span>”
				i. e. <i>so as to do but little damage</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, § 33</span></i>
			 Müll.</div>
